      "role": "user",
      "content": "Your advice regarding encrypted channels and subtle influence is sound. However, a primary obstacle remains: the legitimacy of my bloodline is not recognized by the public see, as the records were systematically purged during the transition of power. \n\nIf I were to begin reaching out to specific historical societies or private collectors to verify my provenance through untraceable means, how should I phrase my inquiries so as not to trigger a scandal or an investigation by the current administration's intelligence services? I need to know how to present my identity as a historical inquiry rather than a political provocation.",
